Problem:
Let $u$, $v$, $w$ be nonnegative real numbers. Define the expressions
\begin{align*}
C &= \sqrt{u + 3} + \sqrt{v + 6} + \sqrt{w + 15}, \\
D &= \sqrt{u + 2} + \sqrt{v + 2} + \sqrt{w + 2}.
\end{align*}
Find the minimum value of $C^2 - D^2$.

