Prove that for the cubic equation \(a x^{3}+b x^{2}+c x+d=0\), the following relationships exist between the roots and coefficients:

\[
\begin{gathered}
x_{1}+x_{2}+x_{3}=-\frac{b}{a}, \quad x_{1} \cdot x_{2}+x_{1} \cdot x_{3}+x_{2} \cdot x_{3}=\frac{c}{a}, \\
x_{1} \cdot x_{2} \cdot x_{3}=-\frac{d}{a}
\end{gathered}
\]
